{
	"character": "Arthur",
	"voice": "am_michael",
	"speed": 0.92,
	"lines": {
		"Ms. Vance. You found us; most people drive past twice. The Harrow manuscript is on your desk. I trust you'll find it... salvageable.": "arthur-286becc585.mp3",
		"The Harrow book. Good bones, a bad second act. I want to know if you see what I see.": "arthur-9447e422e6.mp3",
		"Harrow kills the sister in chapter nine, then spends three chapters pretending it didn't happen. Tell me what you'd cut.": "arthur-ea005da89d.mp3",
		"Eleven books a year. Each one has to earn the paper it's printed on. Most don't, and we print them anyway.": "arthur-639c39236d.mp3",
		"Notes by Friday. In the margins. If I wanted essays, I'd have hired a critic.": "arthur-022f94c0fb.mp3",
		"Read the last page first. If the ending lies, the whole book lies.": "arthur-984d953d4c.mp3",
		"You read the middle. Hardly anyone reads the middle.": "arthur-ba7a3b26c5.mp3",
		"That's the note. That's exactly the note. Write it down before I take the credit.": "arthur-4b352bc4fc.mp3",
		"Trust that instinct. It's rarer in this building than you'd think.": "arthur-60559c6b4d.mp3",
		"Good. You argue with the text, not with me. Keep doing that.": "arthur-6198cc8ee6.mp3",
		"Is there a question about the work in there somewhere?": "arthur-707d5f4c8d.mp3",
		"I don't need encouragement, Ms. Vance. I need a second act.": "arthur-40fa5607d9.mp3",
		"The manuscript. Please.": "arthur-01f7600d96.mp3",
		"There's tea in the kitchen. The kettle sticks. Hit it on the left side. The right side is for lost causes.": "arthur-6674b66ccf.mp3",
		"Welcome to Blackwood. The leaves don't fall here. After a while you stop looking up.": "arthur-2fe924b23a.mp3",
		"The radiator in your office knocks at four o'clock. It isn't a ghost. Probably.": "arthur-5dfa650b77.mp3",
		"You came a long way for a job at a press nobody has heard of. I won't ask why. Not today.": "arthur-d4e591fb9c.mp3",
		"Thank you. I mean that. It's been a long season.": "arthur-2938e7e1ce.mp3",
		"Sit, if you like. The chair is better than it looks. Most things here are.": "arthur-28e0d0a1cd.mp3",
		"I'm not good at first days. Mine or anyone else's. You'll have to forgive me.": "arthur-6915a654ac.mp3",
		"You're easier to talk to than I expected. I'm not sure that's a compliment to either of us.": "arthur-cbb9386693.mp3",
		"Mm.": "arthur-cf4d76c15a.mp3",
		"If that's everything.": "arthur-9788d81449.mp3",
		"Not now.": "arthur-32397652b6.mp3",
		"That's not a conversation for the office.": "arthur-ce9631ffd5.mp3",
		"I'd rather talk about the manuscript. It's the one thing in here I know how to fix.": "arthur-8a478dd9e4.mp3",
		"My private life isn't on the reading list.": "arthur-425ed8e18d.mp3",
		"Some doors in this building stay shut, Ms. Vance. That's one of them.": "arthur-34e0bcb53d.mp3",
		"Not yet. Ask me again some other day. I might surprise us both.": "arthur-5b6c4986f2.mp3",
		"Don't.": "arthur-85cbcffbcb.mp3",
		"Ms. Vance. I said no.": "arthur-12e8c74895.mp3",
		"Margaret. Two years this October, if October ever ends. It came on fast. Weeks, not months. They never gave it a proper name.": "arthur-339d98aa1f.mp3",
		"My wife used to sit where you're sitting. She hated this town's autumn. She said it felt like a waiting room.": "arthur-84dea1a9c4.mp3",
		"She stopped sleeping, near the end. She said someone kept talking to her in the dark. The doctors called it fever.": "arthur-4f70617b2f.mp3",
		"I kept her reading glasses on my desk for a year. Then I put them in a drawer. I still know which drawer.": "arthur-49a2c410d3.mp3",
		"She would have liked you. She liked anyone who argued with me and won.": "arthur-a7250f705e.mp3",
		"That will be all. The manuscript won't edit itself.": "arthur-9e2665e443.mp3",
		"Back to it. Friday, Ms. Vance.": "arthur-8e8f6bcb3f.mp3",
		"Mind the door on your way out. It sticks. Everything here does.": "arthur-12098128e6.mp3",
		"Go on. And... thank you, Elena.": "arthur-6cdf5d4b32.mp3",
		"Go home early. First days are long enough without me in them.": "arthur-cf30da2d21.mp3",
		"We're done here.": "arthur-2f96a6df3c.mp3",
		"Close the door behind you.": "arthur-bd6b97ad48.mp3"
	}
}
